PART 2: components of the container image

The image ghcr.io/restow-backup/cicd-updater contains, besides the bundle above,
these programs, unmodified, from their official distributions (docker/Dockerfile
pins each by digest or takes it from Alpine Linux's signed packages):

- Node.js 24 (MIT, plus the licences of its bundled components listed in
  https://github.com/nodejs/node/blob/main/LICENSE), from the official
  node:24-alpine image.
- Alpine Linux base system (among others musl, MIT, and BusyBox, GPL-2.0, whose
  tar the volume backup uses), https://alpinelinux.org; package sources at
  https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports.
- Docker CLI (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/docker/cli
- Docker Buildx (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/docker/buildx
- Docker Compose (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/docker/compose
  (the three above from the official docker:cli image)
- cosign (Apache-2.0), https://github.com/sigstore/cosign
  (from the official ghcr.io/sigstore/cosign/cosign image)
- age (BSD-3-Clause), https://github.com/FiloSottile/age (Alpine package)
- tini (MIT), https://github.com/krallin/tini (Alpine package)
- ca-certificates (MPL-2.0 for the certificate data), Alpine package

The Apache License 2.0 text is in LICENSE. The licence texts of the Alpine
packages are part of their sources; the BusyBox (GPL-2.0) sources are available
from Alpine Linux as linked above. cicd-updater runs these programs as separate
processes; it does not link them.
